{
  "id": "Compound::DB00617 - Gene::1576",
  "verbalization": "Paramethadione appears to interact with Cyp3a4 through a series of interconnected molecular and enzymatic pathways. The evidence suggests that Paramethadione binds to Cyp2c8, which then participates in oxidoreductive activities, including those involving quinone or similar acceptors. This activity is ultimately linked to Cyp3a4, indicating a potential enzymatic interaction where Cyp2c8 may serve as a mediator in the metabolic activation of Paramethadione. The shared participation of Cyp3a4 in these processes implies a possible role in the biotransformation of Paramethadione, though the exact mechanism of this interaction remains unclear. The evidence highlights a dependency on Cyp2c8 as a bridge between Paramethadione and Cyp3a4, suggesting a broader metabolic pathway that may be relevant to the drug's pharmacological effects.",
